Principal decision: correct only driver filesystem I/O to use extended Windows paths where required. Preserve logical paths and all native repository/resource/tool identity inputs, original artifact refs/digests, link/reparse guards, exclusive writes and containment checks. Cover read_exact and all driver-owned destination/snapshot I/O that can cross the Windows ordinary-path limit, not merely this one existing filename. Never truncate or rename artifacts, alter old bytes, bypass guards, or substitute authority. Native source remains frozen. No driver rerun, source imports, synthetic path fixtures/probes, tests, or new roots during the fix/review. Retain exact preimages and return a bounded diff for independent review before actual preparation retries.
